// Multi-voice augmentation-dot force-down. When two voices collide and the
// DOWN voice has a dotted note sitting ON a staff line, its dot is forced into
// the space BELOW the line (instead of the default space above) to clear the up
// voice. Here the down voice's dotted b (B4, the treble middle line) collides
// with the up voice's un-dotted c' a second above, so the down dot is pushed
// below the line.
// WARNING: forcing DOWN off the staff line is Lily#'s OWN rule. LilyPond's dot-direction
// rule (note-collision.cc:375-398) fires only when the shift is positive and sets UP /
// CENTER / the up chord's direction. This book therefore watches Lily#'s behaviour, not
// LilyPond's; see HANDOFF 2 A. The :411-448 this line used to cite holds no dot code at all.
octave absolute
time 2/4
part p { clef treble }
section Main {
  p {
    voice { c'4 c'4 }
    { b4. b8 }
  }
}
form main { Main }
score main "dot-force-down" { staff p }
